### How to run cellranger count on one sample  ###

# Create a working directory 

$ mkdir cellranger_demo  
$ cd cellranger_demo  

# Make a data directory 
$ mkdir data  

# Make softlinks to the fastq files in the data directory  
NB use the naming convention: 
[Sample Name]_S1_[Read Type]_001.fastq.gz

$ ln -s /path/to/fastq/R1.fastq.gz data/sample1_S1_R1_001.fastq.gz
$ ln -s /path/to/fastq/R2.fastq.gz data/sample1_S1_R1_001.fastq.gz

# Make softlinks to the genome reference 

$  ln -s /project/ancestryhca/shared/chromium/analysis/20250926_Zim_soft_tissue_cellranger/refdata-gex-GRCh38-2020-A/ .

# Copy the slurm template file 
$ cp /project/ancestryhca/shared/chromium/analysis/20251002_Zim_soft_tissue_cellranger_cluster/slurm.template .

# Copy and update the cellranger count slurm script  
--id will be the name of the output directory 
--sample is the sample name that has to match the start of the fastq files e.g. sample1
$ cp /project/tendonhca/ccohen/teaching/TENET_snRNAseq/cellranger_count.sh 

Run the job 
$ sbatch cellranger_count.sh
